fresh-eyes: independent cold reviewer (subagent, no authorship of this branch), full scope of the three commits moving the reference and SKILL.md reads onto the mdstore capability.

Verdict LAND on this tip, 05d5b60.

Two rounds. Round one returned DO-NOT-LAND on four items, and found a
real hole rather than a test gap: a handle confines the names used
under a root and does not choose the root, so a library shipping
'references -> /etc' chose it and almanac show served /etc/hosts. The
predicate this branch replaced had the same hole, so it was inherited.
Three names in the escape loop asserted nothing, and one comment
claimed the old predicate followed an outward link when it refused it.

Round two blocked again on the listing: the read path was fixed and
append_file_references seven lines below still followed the link,
enumerating 61 filenames out of /etc into an agent's context. Names
only, since content was already refused, but the two halves disagreed
about what existed, so an agent was told to run commands show rejects.

Round three verified by execution. The enumeration returns 0 names. The
reviewer built a references directory holding one of every entry type
and diffed the listing against what show serves for each: no
disagreement in either direction. Every guard has a named test that
dies when the guard dies. parse_skill_md takes one parameter, so the
reproduction where an entry reported a path whose bytes it never read
no longer compiles.

76 tests, clippy clean, fmt clean, missouri 7 passed 0 failed, 121
assertions.

Open, none blocking, each filed: a check-then-open race two syscalls
wide, measured at 0 wins in 40000 attempts and 45 in 2000 with the
window widened; a hard link out of the references directory, which has
no target to inspect; a comment that claims the listing and show apply
the same test when a third path is what makes them agree; and a named
pipe in a skill directory hanging almanac and the MCP server forever,
which predates this work.
